{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":46.290000915527344,"text":"Montmartre is the highest hill in Paris, 130 meters, and for a long time it was a village of windmills and vineyards. After hard years for the city in the 1870s, local people promised to build a church up there and paid for it with countless small donations. Building took almost 40 years. The church is startlingly white, and nobody paints it. Its stone comes from one particular quarry and has an unusual property. When it gets wet, it releases a substance that acts like whitewash and rinses the dirt away. So rain, which blackens every other building in Paris, cleans this one. The hill underneath is riddled with old gypsum quarries, which is why 83 deep shafts had to be filled with concrete before the first stone was laid.","words":[{"word":"Montmartre","start":0,"end":0.7400000095367432},{"word":"is","start":0.7400000095367432,"end":1.0800000429153442},{"word":"the","start":1.0800000429153442,"end":1.5399999618530273},{"word":"highest","start":1.5399999618530273,"end":1.7400000095367432},{"word":"hill","start":1.7400000095367432,"end":1.940000057220459},{"word":"in","start":1.940000057220459,"end":2.5399999618530273},{"word":"Paris","start":2.5399999618530273,"end":2.5399999618530273},{"word":"130","start":3.0199999809265137,"end":3.680000066757202},{"word":"meters","start":3.680000066757202,"end":4.019999980926514},{"word":"and","start":4.480000019073486,"end":4.760000228881836},{"word":"for","start":4.760000228881836,"end":4.920000076293945},{"word":"a","start":4.920000076293945,"end":5.079999923706055},{"word":"long","start":5.079999923706055,"end":5.239999771118164},{"word":"time","start":5.239999771118164,"end":5.519999980926514},{"word":"it","start":5.519999980926514,"end":5.699999809265137},{"word":"was","start":5.699999809265137,"end":5.840000152587891},{"word":"a","start":5.840000152587891,"end":6.320000171661377},{"word":"village","start":6.320000171661377,"end":6.32000017166137